Z||000000||Ayrow||11-22-2001||02:11 AM||||Hi everybody, from Norfolk, VA!!!<P>I tried this once before, but I don't think it went through.  <P>I found this forum about two weeks ago and have fallen in love with it!  You guys are awesome!<P>I have owned 4 Fieros in my lifetime and currently have an '87 Blue GT in storage (drained fluids, on blocks) that will remain there.<BR>I have been out of the Fiero game for about ten years and am about to get back into it in a big way.<BR>I'm looking for an '88 GT that I can restore and have fun with.<P>Here's my question:  If you were talking to a guy that knew the Fiero's ins-and-outs several years ago (like me) but he was overwhelmed by all of the new things people are doing to their Fieros (technology, mods, etc..) what would you say are the MUST-HAVE modifications every Fiero should have if it were to be restored?<P>I want to make the right desicions on these things and am very interested in your input.<P>Thanks guys.  I hope to be a big part of your family here.<P>Ayrow<P>PS..You can see pics of my some of my Fieros and other cars here: <A HREF="http://www.ayrow.com/fiero.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.ayrow.com/fiero.html</A> ||||reg||10
Z||000001||Haze_Performance||11-22-2001||02:35 AM||||Welcome back to the Fiero world.. & Welcome to the Forum..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Well, after the restoration the mods are pretty much a matter of taste. Theres a lot of people here that are into body mods & not engine. (& vise versa) You'll surely find the mods that you like here.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> Good luck..<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>-Haze <BR>(If your looking for links, I have a few parts links on the old website..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> )<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/goodlife.gif">    <BR><FONT SIZE="1"><FONT COLOR="purple">Goto Website - <A HREF="http://www.ClassicFiero.com" TARGET=_blank>Click Here</A> </FONT></FONT>||||reg||14
Z||000002||Joe Torma||11-22-2001||02:40 AM||||WELCOME!<P>Mods...no mods here, well none that are finished!  I say its gotta go fast before it can look fast and then it can sound fast.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/simplesig1.gif">  <BR>Did you get your car in my book yet????<BR> <A HREF="http://www.animatedconcepts.com/fierobook.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.animatedconcepts.com/fierobook.htm</A>||||reg||6
Z||000003||DR650SE||11-22-2001||02:52 AM||||WELCOME BACK!! I just want to say That tonight I talked to a guy I went to high school with.  He graduated a few years before me and i graduated two years ago.  He too wrecked his fiero.  He said one thing is for sure.  I will have another.  I'm glad to see you have to.  A wise man on this forum once said something to the extent of "there are only two permanent things, herpes and fieros."  Glad to see you got the fieros part.  I got It as well.  Now to your question.  One thing I like thatr people are doing now is makeing there fiero unique.  The many differant body mods that are out there to the engines.  I really like the cadillac northstar system.  I only have two fieros and would like to put a northstar in.  The kit to do it from v8archie costs about $2-3k.  Thats not including the motor, tranny, ect.  Those you can get from a junkyard or ebay.  My first chance I get I will try and install a turbo on my 2.8L.  What ever you do, do it because you like it.  Theres no right or wrong.  What ever you decide, keep us updated.  I would love to see more pics of your cars.  I also love the motorcycle you had as well as all your other cars.  Especially the 3000GT twin turbo.  Nice car.  Again, welcome back.<P>------------------<BR>AIM:  DR650SE<BR>2 Black 86 SE's V-6 4-SPD||||reg||14
Z||000004||Ayrow||11-22-2001||03:59 AM||||Thanks guys.<P>I updated the page tonight and included most of the 16 vehicles I have owned on it, including my Fieros.<P>Talk about funny.  I had forgotten about all of the vehicles I have been through, and I'm only 32!!!<BR>LOL<P>I'm not so interested in doing ridiculous modifications as I am in just finding a car and gettting it "up-to-date" and as reliable and fun as possible - whether it be done by using "old" parts, or new ones from this generation. <P>Putting a new engine (Caddy, Chevy V8, etc) is not out of the question.  I'm just not sure if I can afford it.<BR>Is it a good idea to keep the 2.8 and just restore/rebuild it, or would I be better moving up?<P>These are the things I am concerned about....<P>Ok, it wouldn't hurt to have it turn heads either, I suppose.  ;-)<P>Thanks again,<P>Ayrow<BR> <A HREF="http://www.ayrow.com/fiero.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.ayrow.com/fiero.html</A> ||||reg||12
